T034 (W1.2, the simulation in a real Web Worker, with the App wiring behind ?simworker=1): cloud/t034, cloud carry-over Nov 3, review fix round Nov 3; report docs/dev/reports/local-W1.2-worker.md; tsc clean, full vitest 2,174 passed, bot 192,899 (dev's reference since B3); tools/qa-worker.mjs on the production build at size 256 with 10-minute soaks: 39 of 39 with ?simwasm=wasm, 35 of 37 without (the 2 FAILs the harness's own, fixed and passed in the wasm run).
Open, for the lead: (1) §6's "worker's protector intact after 10 min" cannot be observed in Chromium 153, whose V8 has no ArrayBufferDetaching protector (decision 11; qa-worker gates it automatically on a V8 that has one); (2) real-GPU numbers: the freeze test's 1 s, boot time, FPS with the worker; (3) the G6 window (a crash between the worker's Ready and the scene) is covered by code only; (4) T039 (W1.3): the worker's journal, its IndexedDB and boot replay; (5) FallbackWorldView / FallbackObjectsView still miss a resync (decision 9).
